<Events>

	<Event side="0" repeat="1">
		<Trigger type="turn" data1="1"/>
		<Message>You must defeat the various factions of dragons in the Dragon Realm to gain access to Kelthurax&apos;s cave.  Only then will you be able to ask Kelthurax about the Sundering.</Message>
	</Event>

	<Event side="0" repeat="1">
		<Trigger type="turn" data1="2"/>
		<Message>It seems that the word is out that you carry the Dragonstone. | The dragons in this land will stop at nothing to get it back. Your way to Kelthurax may be harder than it first seemed.</Message>
	</Event>

	<Event side="0" repeat="1">
		<Trigger type="turn" data1="3"/>
		<Message>A Dragonslayer, named Ivan Wyrmsbane, arrives in your capital. | Ivan offers to help you. He tells you that a set of 3 different-colored skulls from some larger dragons, typically found in ruins, can be fashioned into a mana crystal.</Message>
		<Action type="unit" data1="0" data2="1" data3="14" string1="Ivan Wyrmsbane"/>
	</Event>

	<Ruin id="0" available_for_quest="no">
		<Heading>Swamp Dragon</Heading>
		<Message>This dragon has a large treasure hoard of gems, jewellery and coins.</Message>
		<Monster type="49" number="1" level="6"/>
		<Reward type="gold" data="2000"/>
	</Ruin >
	<Ruin id="1" available_for_quest="no">
		<Heading>Storm Dragon</Heading>
		<Message>This dragon has a huge treasure hoard of gems, jewellery and coins.</Message>
		<Monster type="50" number="1" level="7"/>
		<Reward type="gold" data="2500"/>
	</Ruin >
	<Ruin id="2" available_for_quest="no">
		<Heading>Fire Dragon</Heading>
		<Message>This dragon has a massive treasure hoard of gems, jewellery and coins.</Message>
		<Monster type="52" number="1" level="8"/>
		<Reward type="gold" data="3000"/>
	</Ruin >
